       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Just a note re: supporting this at the low level:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "One approach we've talked about is to use exceptions as a way to trigger this condition at the Akubra level.  It would be fairly easy to do this with a hierarchical-storage aware Akubra plugin that threw a Fedora-recognized subclass of IOException in cases where Blob.openInputStream is called.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://fedora-commons.org/bamboo/browse/AKUBRA-SAN/latest/artifact/site/apidocs/org/akubraproject/Blob.html#openInputStream%28%29"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://fedora-commons.org/bamboo/browse/AKUBRA-SAN/latest/artifact/site/apidocs/org/akubraproject/Blob.html#openInputStream%28%29",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "...without changing today's Akubra API.  If this approach works out, we could add such an exception to the formal Akubra api, on par with exceptions like MissingBlobException, DuplicateBlobException, etc.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
