      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Just a note re: supporting this at the low level:</p>\n\n<p>One approach we've talked about is to use exceptions as a way to trigger this condition at the Akubra level.  It would be fairly easy to do this with a hierarchical-storage aware Akubra plugin that threw a Fedora-recognized subclass of IOException in cases where Blob.openInputStream is called.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-commons.org/bamboo/browse/AKUBRA-SAN/latest/artifact/site/apidocs/org/akubraproject/Blob.html#openInputStream%28%29\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-commons.org/bamboo/browse/AKUBRA-SAN/latest/artifact/site/apidocs/org/akubraproject/Blob.html#openInputStream%28%29</a></p>\n\n<p>...without changing today's Akubra API.  If this approach works out, we could add such an exception to the formal Akubra api, on par with exceptions like MissingBlobException, DuplicateBlobException, etc.</p>",
     "created": "12/Mar/10 4:51 PM",
     "id": "11258",
     "jsdPublic": true,
